aused and it was  incredibly reckless and foolish on my  behalf  and so i want to apologize for that  apologize to the club for the  embarrassment it would have caused them  with regards to the allegations about  the dog there's it's an ongoing  investigation at the club  um so i can't go into detail with that  but i want to reiterate what i said in  my statement um  the other day you know and finally i you  know i deplore  all forms of racism and discrimination  the man at the center of this azim rafiq  has reiterated his apologies for  anti-semitic messages he shared as a 19  year old  nobody in cricket has come out of this  well the game has to change and show  everybody there's no going back  tom parmenter sky news south london
 

